Thanks all. Writing down what we know so far, proper RCA to follow.

What happened: The payment-gateway API key expired at 00:00 UTC. orders-api g=
ot 401 from the payment provider for every card payment for 51 minutes, until=
 the key was rotated.
Impact: 51 minutes without card payments. About 1,900 checkout attempts faile=
d.

Timeline (UTC):
2026-05-02 00:00 Payment API key expired. None. The expiry reminder went to a=
n old mailbox.
2026-05-02 00:07 Alert PaymentAuthFailures fired. On-call opened an incident.
2026-05-02 00:31 On-call found the expired key with shopctl secrets describe.=
 Paged the payments team on-call for the rotate permission.
2026-05-02 00:52 Key rotated and orders-api restarted. Watched the 401 rate f=
all to zero.
2026-05-02 00:58 Card payments working again. Closed the incident.

Root cause: The key expiry reminder went to an unmonitored mailbox, so the ke=
y expired unnoticed. Nothing alerted on keys close to expiry.
Fix: Rotated the key with shopctl and restarted orders-api.

Follow ups:
- Send key expiry reminders to the payments team group address. (Payments tea=
m)
- Alert 14 days before any third-party key expires. (SRE team)
- Give the SRE on-call permission to rotate the payment key. (Payments team)

new key after rotation is pk_canary_5d2e9b7f1a4c8e3b, old one gets revoked to=
morrow

